WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:13.330
Hello, this is Don Byron coming
to you from my palatial home

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:14.440
in upstate New York.

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:20.410
These three pieces
that I wrote are

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:25.765
inspired by another
native Bronx, like myself.

00:00:25.765 --> 00:00:28.900
The great Saul Bass.

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:35.170
Bass is-- if you've seen
his work, you remember it.

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:39.340
He's the person that really
updated the whole vibe of what

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:42.490
you could do in the title
sequence of a movie,

00:00:42.490 --> 00:00:46.630
and he starts with Otto
Preminger's great works

00:00:46.630 --> 00:00:50.820
like "Man with the Golden
Arm," and continues

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:54.570
through not just doing
Hitchcock's stuff,

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:59.670
but actually being an influence
to the way it was made.

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:03.970
He won an Oscar for a short.

00:01:03.970 --> 00:01:07.510
He designed several
of the corporate logos

00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:12.970
to businesses like Bell
Telephone and United Airlines,

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:18.370
and for someone like me who's
a student of film music,

00:01:18.370 --> 00:01:25.240
he's an important part of how we
get masterworks like Spartacus

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:32.540
and Psycho, North by
Northwest, all of those things

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:38.310
are shaped by this person, both
graphically and artistically.

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:41.360
So me, as a film composer,
which is what I really

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:47.630
think that I am, I just
decided to tackle 10 of these,

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:50.940
and these are the
first three, and I

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:55.380
thank MIT for commissioning them
and giving me the opportunity

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:57.550
to work on this music.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:00.400
And that's what
these pieces are.

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:04.960
I mean, my influences, as
a musician and composer,

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:10.509
are pretty wide, but Saul
Bass, who actually grew up

00:02:10.509 --> 00:02:13.240
less than a mile from
my parents' house

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:17.890
in the Bronx, which also means
he grew up less than a mile

00:02:17.890 --> 00:02:21.340
from the place where
Abner Louima was shot.

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:25.290
So that's what this piece
is, and I hope you enjoy it.

